{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And there you shall serve elohim</b> — from the moment you serve their worshippers, you serve them. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 4:28). And I have already explained its secret: that one who dwells outside the Land is as though he serves idolatry and the work of human hands, from above to below, as I mentioned in the section of Acharei Mot (Leviticus 18:25)." "And the reason for <b>they do not eat and do not smell</b> is to say that they are inert stone as they were from the beginning; there is in them no spirit of life at all, not even the life of a human being. For at first he said 'they do not see and do not hear,' to say that they are no god, and they do not see the affliction of their servants, and they do not hear their prayer, and from their distress they do not deliver them. And he returned and said that even diminished life, such as the life of a human being, is not in them — and behold, the one who made them is more honorable than them. Or the reason of the verse may be understood against the honor of the Most High, to say: they do not see the distress of their servants and do not hear their prayer, and they do not eat — that no fire goes forth from before them and consumes their offerings, and they do not smell — the pleasing fragrance of their offerings. And Scripture employed indefinite language, for these senses are not in them at all."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase 'from above to below' (מלמעלה למטה) is rendered hyper-literally; it belongs to the kabbalistic passage and is left cryptic per the translator's mandate."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:22.863521503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}